/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Local-only working notes (review trackers, scratch plans)
*.local.md

# proptest's failing-seed corpus. We don't persist it: CI explores fresh
# random cases each run, and a committed file is easy to populate with
# noise (e.g. seeds from a deliberately-broken local experiment). If a
# real shrink is worth pinning, add it as an explicit unit test instead.
proptest-regressions/

# Claude Code harness runtime state (e.g. the scheduled-task lock). Per-session
# transient — not project source — so it shouldn't be tracked. Scoped to the
# lock file rather than all of .claude/ so intentional project config (e.g. a
# committed settings.json) can still be added later.
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# reflow2's local design graph (machine state; the durable record is an export)
.reflow2/
# reflow2's MCP configs — they carry an absolute path to YOUR binary
.mcp.json
opencode.json
.vscode/mcp.json
# reflow2's loop-nudge hook — an absolute path to YOUR kit
.claude/settings.local.json
